        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "media": {
            "duration": 6049,
            "fileSize": 98046330
          },
          "note": "Marketplace",
          "description": "Dare to join Finnian Jones as he ushers Thomas into the legendary world of Sir Malcolm and the Missing Prince, a place of history, mystery, and new beginnings.  \n\nJoin Sir Malcolm as he encounters a battle raging in the heart of his king. Prince Hubert, proven to be an unworthy heir, will destroy the kingdom if allowed to rise to power. Through the bold intervention of the king’s most trusted knight, Sir Malcolm, a plan to teach the prince a lesson he will never forget is about to unfold. Before the plan can be carried out, however, Sir Malcolm must convince the king that his plan is for the greater good of both his son and the kingdom. \n\nAs the plot thickens, far from the safety of the palace, Hubert now known as Hugh, has exchanged his princely apparel for rags, leaving all his royal advantages behind. In a remote village where people work to eat, Hugh must learn that the requirement for kingship is sacrifice and servanthood. \n\nIt is with great enthusiasm and anticipation that we introduce to you Sir Malcolm and the Missing Prince, an exhilarating and suspenseful masterpiece for all ages.  \n\nHosted by John Rhys-Davies from The Lord of the Rings!\n\nWhat is Lamplighter Theatre? Lamplighter Theatre audio dramas are adapted from our rare collection of character-building books, currently heard by a million listeners weekly in 34 countries. Riveting music, engaging sound effects, and world-class talent, all combine in gripping dramas that inspire virtue, reinforce moral values, and ignite the theatre of the mind. ",
          "author": "Lamplighter Theatre",
